Z||000000||voyagerspe||03-26-2001||01:00 AM||||OK, Ive got to set the scene.  Im leaving work at about 11:00pm on a sunday night.  Theres hardly anyone on the road.  I stop for gas (this is only my 1st fill up on my new motor(3.4)).  When I go in to pay for the gas <BR>the girl working there is to busy talking to her boyfriend to take my 10 bucks.  So I just  leave it on the counter and leave, of course  her boyfriend makes some smart comment that I didnt quite hear(I just walked out).  Im right about to jump into the car and go home when I remember to check my oil, Its a very fresh motor about 200 miles on it.  I check the oil(its good) then I notice the boyfriend <BR>jumping into a new bonnieville ssei(must be dads car).  As I leave sure enuff hes on my tale, I stop at the first light, hes next to me gunning the motor.  Im thinking crap this is a fresh motor and I dont want to beat it yet, then I think oh what the hell why not.  <BR>The light changes we both stand on it He smokes the tires, his tires scream but never bite in.  I on the other hand have a little chirp and am down the road.  I slow down when I hit about 80 but hes way back.  I come up on another red light and hes coming up along side of me just when I think hes about to rematch he puts on his blinker and pulls into an Arby's.  Talk about poetic justice not only did I get to toast some punk with a smart mouth, I showed him up with a fiero when his should have blown my doors off.   ||||reg||14
Z||000001||GT Bastard||03-26-2001||01:07 AM||||The one thing I've learned from street racing my fiero's is that they can LAUNCH.  I think it also serves to intimidate others when you jump ahead from the get-go.  Good kill.||||reg||1
